.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
SDL3 window and presentation\&. 

Internal header\&. This layer owns the window, the CPU pixel buffer that ThorVG rasterizes into, and the texture that buffer is uploaded to\&. It does not draw anything itself\&.
.PP
Presentation is deliberately dumb: upload the changed rectangle, draw one textured quad, present\&. The same path serves every target, so there is no GPU renderer to keep in sync with a software one\&.
.PP
Platform input is turned into toolkit events here and handed to the router, which is what decides where each one lands\&. Nothing in this layer knows what a widget is\&.
.PP
\fBNot part of the host facing interface\&.\fP The platform layer\&. A host binds to \fBschultz_api\&.h\fP; this header is the toolkit's own and may change without notice\&. 
.PP
Definition in file \fBschultz_sdl\&.h\fP\&.
